WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.902 line:0%
-Jack, looking great, buddy.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.870 line:0%
-[ Sighs ] This is so lovely.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.705 line:0%
I have a chance
to put on a suit.

00:00:06.705 --> 00:00:08.841 line:0%
That has been a rarity of late,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:12.345 line:0%
and some human contact, as well,
which is just a joy.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.380 line:0%
-You look like
you're feeling better.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.215 line:0%
I know that you had coronavirus.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.817 line:0%
I'm sorry about that.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.852 line:0%
What was it like? I mean --

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.488 line:0%
-I had it early! I was, like --

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:25.524 line:0%
I had, like, pre-Tom Hanks
coronavirus,

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.660 line:0%
before celebrities
were even getting it.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.063 line:0%
And I had it in the first week
of lockdown, and it was --

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.631 line:0%
Yeah, it was like --
I had it pretty bad,

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:34.433 line:0%
and I think I'm quite fit
and healthy.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.770 line:0%
And I'd seen my parents just
before the lockdown had started,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.072 line:0%
so I was terrified
that I gave it to them.

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:43.943 line:0%
And it was -- Yeah. It's real.
Wash your hands. Wear a mask.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.145 line:0%
-Yep. How is your dad doing,
by the way?

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.180 line:0%
We always talk about your dad
when you're on the show.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.815 line:0%
-Yeah. [ Chuckles ]

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.251 line:0%
Yeah, it's been weird.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:55.055 line:0%
I-I haven't been able
to hug him for...

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:59.358 line:0%
31 years, and so now --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:01.561 line:0%
Oh, we got to work on that.
We got to work on that.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.930 line:0%
-Yeah. We have a --
-Are you able to see him at all?

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.166 line:0%
Do you get to see him, or --
socially distant?

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.003 line:0%
-Yeah, I actually did
a Father's Day special

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.705 line:0%
for the BBC,
which we filmed at his house.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.641 line:0%
I was in the garden,
and he was in the house.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.376 line:0%
And I did a load of, like,
Father's Day surprises for him.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:21.013 line:0%
So, I got, like, a big brass
band outside his bedroom window

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.382 line:0%
at 6:00 in the morning to play
"The Dam Busters" theme tune,

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.217 line:0%
which is his favorite song,
although turns out

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.586 line:0%
not his favorite song
at 6:00 in the morning.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:30.156 line:0%
And then I was worried
that he wasn't gonna be able

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.457 line:0%
to kind of travel
the world with me,

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.092 line:0%
which is something
that he loves doing,

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.261 line:0%
and I was sad that he was
gonna be stuck in the house,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.862 line:0%
and I thought he was
a little bit like

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:39.165 line:0%
the little, old man from "Up,"
and that got me thinking.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.233 line:0%
So then my second
surprise for him

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:46.606 line:0%
was that I put like 300 balloons
on the roof of his house.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.474 line:0%
I was like, "This is amazing!

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.842 line:0%
This is an amazing
Father's Day gift,"

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.877 line:0%
but he did not see it that way.
-That is brilliant!

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:56.182 line:0%
How are you not being able
to travel and see other people

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.351 line:0%
and, you know -- 'cause you're
always out doing stuff.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:02.221 line:0%
Are you getting used
to being by yourself?

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.124 line:0%
-Yeah, I mean, now
our sort of lockdown is over,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.794 line:0%
and people are going
back into real life.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.497 line:0%
Gyms are open this week, which
is, like, a big thing for --

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.400 line:0%
I mean, not for me.
I'm not much of a gym guy.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.202 line:0%
-Oh, really?
-I actually --

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.605 line:0%
[ Chuckling ] Yeah, thank you
for faking surprise there.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.741 line:0%
-That's my acting --
That's my acting --

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.875 line:0%
No, you're --

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.444 line:0%
-That is exceptional
acting work, Jimmy.

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:29.181 line:0%
Like, this -- I'll put it down
to a delay on the connection,

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:31.684 line:0%
but that was way -- "Really?"

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:35.188 line:0%
You're a great host
and a wonderful actor,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.624 line:0%
but that was not even believable
for like a split-second.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.092 line:0%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:41.493 line:0%
-No, I --
-This suit is cut very well,

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:43.596 line:0%
but beneath it,
I have a body that looks like

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:47.400 line:0%
it's been drawn by a child.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.734 line:0%
-I do go to the gym, though.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.937 line:0%
I just don't, like --
I'm not, like, a weights guy.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.372 line:0%
I actually --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.174 line:0%
I have a story I'll tell you.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.609 line:0%
I was in a gym once,

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.544 line:0%
and it reminds me
'cause I'm wearing these.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.578 line:0%
'Cause I don't know about you.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.080 line:0%
I have this problem
with AirPods.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.516 line:0%
I do it all the time now,
where I don't realize

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.819 line:0%
that my AirPods have not synched
to my mobile phone,

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.022 line:0%
and my music is, like,
playing to everyone.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.389 line:0%
-Oh, yes.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:11.691 line:0%
-Do you ever do that?
-Yes, of course.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.059 line:0%
Yeah, I've done that.
Absolutely, yeah.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.094 line:0%
Like, the Bluetooth
doesn't kick in.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.429 line:0%
-Yeah, and you're just,
like, sat there,

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.830 line:0%
and everyone's looking at you.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.800 line:0%
And it's awful, 'cause I also
have terrible music taste.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.167 line:0%
But I had it in the gym.

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.369 line:0%
When I go to the gym,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.538 line:0%
I find a little exercise bike
in the corner.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.906 line:0%
I put on a hoodie.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:30.510 line:0%
I get like incline 0.5,
and I put on something mellow,

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.379 line:0%
like a kind of --
like an audiobook.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.448 line:0%
I like classical music,
film scores.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.982 line:0%
-Really?
-And then I have a little --

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:38.151 line:0%
just a little pootle,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.852 line:0%
like, a quiet, little pootle
in the corner

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.122 line:0%
like a little, old lady
cycling to the grocery store.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:46.092 line:0%
And I was doing it. I'm there
with the hoodie on and things --

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.126 line:0%
and everyone is looking at me.

00:03:48.126 --> 00:03:51.530 line:0%
And, like, my initial thought
for some reason was like,

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.965 line:0%
"Wow, they must all
be looking over here

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:57.035 line:0%
'cause Quadzilla's burning
some serious rubber."

00:03:57.035 --> 00:03:59.438 line:0%
And then I had a slow moment
where it dawned upon me

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.908 line:0%
that the actual reason everyone
in this gym was looking at me

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.243 line:0%
is that I was on a bike,
hoodie up, AirPods in,

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:07.547 line:0%
playing to the entire gym
the theme tune from "E.T."

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:10.349 line:0%
Just there --
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.318 line:0%
You were Elliott!
You were Elliott!

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.254 line:0%
-I'm Elliott! I'm like,
I cannot go back to that gym.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.157 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.
That's perfect.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.759 line:0%
That is perfect. Oh, my gosh.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.228 line:0%
Hey, I love --
I love the special.

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:25.964 line:0%
It's called "I'm Only Joking."
In the special,

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:27.833 line:0%
you talk about your worst gig,
which we've talked about.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:30.002 line:0%
I don't want to spoil it, but
it involves the royal family,

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.238 line:0%
and it's a great story.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.074 line:0%
It's so embarrassing
and awesome.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.677 line:0%
What would you think
is your second-worst gig?

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.411 line:0%
-I think my second-worst gig

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.447 line:0%
should have been
the best gig ever,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.950 line:0%
but I made the fatal error of
thinking that it would be that.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.451 line:0%
And it's when
I got asked to perform

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.787 line:0%
for my soccer team, Arsenal.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:50.155 line:0%
And you're a big sports fan.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:51.891 line:0%
You support the Red Sox?

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.159 line:0%
Have you performed for them?

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:56.362 line:0%
-No, I would never do that.
I don't think -- No.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.798 line:0%
I would never do it.
-I needed that advice,

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.000 line:0%
'cause I was young. I was naive.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.868 line:0%
I was like,
"This'll be amazing."

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.036 line:0%
I was asked to perform

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.804 line:0%
at the Christmas party
for my soccer team.

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:08.708 line:0%
-I don't think the Red Sox
would know who I am.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.442 line:0%
-Well, the Arsenal team

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:12.311 line:0%
definitely did not know
who I am.

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:14.413 line:0%
I arrived for
the Christmas party.

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:15.681 line:0%
I went into the venue.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:19.084 line:0%
The organizer took me downstairs
to a bowling alley,

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:20.886 line:0%
and I was like, "Oh, so --
Where's the stage

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:21.987 line:0%
that I'm performing on?"

00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:23.756 line:0%
She went, "Oh,
it's not so much a gig.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.324 line:0%
It's -- They're here to bowl.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:26.859 line:0%
We just thought we could
give you a microphone,

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.061 line:0%
and you could crack some jokes
whilst they're bowling."

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:32.198 line:0%
I was like, "That is
definitely not a thing."

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.700 line:0%
-This hurts me --
This hurts me just hearing this.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.302 line:0%
-I know. You -- As someone
that's done comedy,

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:40.105 line:0%
you can understand
how horrific this was.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:43.476 line:0%
I stood there with a microphone
at the side of a bowling lane

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.110 line:0%
as all of my heroes bowled,

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.346 line:0%
and I was, like, heckling them
from the side.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:48.747 line:0%
None of them knew
I was a comedian

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.616 line:0%
or that I'd been booked
to do stand-up,

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.718 line:0%
so they thought I was
an employee of the venue.

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.052 line:0%
They were looking
over at me going,

00:05:54.052 --> 00:05:57.223 line:0%
"This bowling alley guy
is a little over-familiar."

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.826 line:0%
[ Laughing ] And then --
Then after that --

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:01.894 line:0%
It got worse,
'cause after the bowling,

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.563 line:0%
they went through
to the next room,

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.397 line:0%
where they had
a karaoke machine set up,

00:06:05.397 --> 00:06:08.066 line:0%
'cause that was the next part
of the evening's festivities.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:09.568 line:0%
Because I'd been
on the microphone,

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:11.169 line:0%
they assumed I was
employed by the venue,

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:13.038 line:0%
so the club captain,
Mikel Arteta, one of my heroes,

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:14.407 line:0%
comes up to me. He's like,

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:16.475 line:0%
"Oh, here's a list of all
the songs that we want played."

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:17.977 line:0%
I was like, "Oh, no, no,
I'm the comedian."

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.545 line:0%
He was like, "Mate, can you
just put on 'Despacito'?"

00:06:20.545 --> 00:06:22.415 line:0%
So then I became
the karaoke deejay

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.483 line:0%
for the rest of the night.
One of the players came over

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:27.019 line:0%
and complained to me
that the pizza bites were cold.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.021 line:0%
I was like, "I don't work here!

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.124 line:0%
I am a professional comedian!

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.458 line:0%
I've played Wembley!"
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:35.494 line:0%
-I was getting their coats
by the end of the night.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:36.862 line:0%
It was horrific, Jimmy.

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:38.764 line:0%
-Also in the special,
by the way, I love --

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:44.003 line:0%
There's an awkward moment
with two humans in the audience,

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:46.272 line:0%
if you know
what I'm talking about.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.474 line:0%
Can you explain what happened?

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:51.144 line:0%
And that was --
It was a magic moment.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.979 line:0%
-It was -- It was a -- Yeah.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.181 line:0%
The comedy gods
were looking down on me.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.950 line:0%
I was doing a bit in the show

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.720 line:0%
where I was talking
about safe sex,

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.089 line:0%
you know, safety first.

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:05.824 line:0%
And I was telling
a cautionary tale

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:09.628 line:0%
about a friend of mine
who had had a one-night stand,

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:14.600 line:0%
and he got the one
that you can't get rid of --

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.767 line:0%
kids.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:18.504 line:0%
-Oh, yeah.
-True story. True story.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:20.238 line:0%
I tell that bit.

00:07:20.238 --> 00:07:24.510 line:0%
I look out into the front row,
and I see this old guy

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.744 line:0%
turn to his daughter

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:28.247 line:0%
and, like, give her,
like, a dig in the ribs.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.549 line:0%
And I should have let it go,
but I couldn't.

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:35.654 line:0%
I was like, "Wow, did you just
nudge your daughter

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.256 line:0%
after I did that joke?"

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:40.392 line:0%
And he looked really mortified.
And I looked at the daughter,

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:43.262 line:0%
and the daughter was giving it,
like, the full Beyoncé,

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.430 line:0%
pointing at the wedding ring.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.165 line:0%
It was his wife.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.232 line:0%
Camera cuts to them,

00:07:47.232 --> 00:07:49.701 line:0%
15,000 people,
like, in hysterics.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:52.204 line:0%
I couldn't speak.
I was so embarrassed

00:07:52.204 --> 00:07:54.206 line:0%
that I'd called out this guy.

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:55.607 line:0%
-It's perfect.
-I mean, to be fair,

00:07:55.607 --> 00:07:59.311 line:0%
if you've got, like, a creepy
age gap in a relationship,

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:01.247 line:0%
do not sit in the front row
of a comedy show

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:03.315 line:0%
for a Netflix live recording.

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:04.950 line:0%
You're only asking for it.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.953 line:0%
But it's in the show,
and, I mean,

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:09.588 line:0%
hopefully they are
still a couple

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:10.956 line:0%
and I haven't
ruined their lives.

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.525 line:0%
But it was -- I couldn't speak
for like two minutes.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:14.593 line:0%
Watch it. Like, you --

00:08:14.593 --> 00:08:16.094 line:0%
I was wearing so much makeup,

00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:17.563 line:0%
you can genuinely
see me change color.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:18.797 line:0%
I was that embarrassed.

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:21.100 line:0%
-I want to show everyone a clip
from the special.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.502 line:0%
Here's a look at,
"I'm Only Joking."

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:27.206 line:0%
-No one in this entire
10,000-strong arena

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:30.876 line:0%
has ever made
a decent piece of toast

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:35.280 line:0%
on the hotel
conveyor belt toaster.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.651 line:0%
Unfathomably [bleep]

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:42.221 line:0%
and handily fitted
with a small window

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:47.159 line:0%
so you can witness your misery
play out in slow-motion.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.494 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:51.163 line:0%
First time through.

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:55.401 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.470 line:0%
[ Whooshes ]

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.005 line:0%
Still bread.

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:01.373 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.373 --> 00:09:04.643 line:0%
Second time through.

00:09:04.643 --> 00:09:06.045 line:0%
[ Whooshes ]

